#+TITLE: @atoz — Wiki concept-graph specialist console
#+SUPERSET_DASHBOARD: atoz-console
#+SUPERSET_DATABASE: org-llm
#+FILETAGS: :template:superset:dashboard:atoz:specialist:
#+OPTIONS: toc:nil num:nil

# Specialist console for @atoz (Wiki concept-graph specialist). Designed by
# @geordi via deepseek-r1 askbook on 2026-05-07. Each chart's
# metric is verbatim from org_llm/metrics/registry.yaml.

* LLM Model Performance Over Time
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: line
:END:

Tracks the average response time of different LLM models over days to
identify performance trends and potential degraded models.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name llm_model_performance_over_time :metric llm_avg_ms :group_by [model, llm_day]
SELECT model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS llm_day, AVG(duration_ms) AS llm_avg_ms FROM llm_calls GROUP BY model, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Crew Actions by Agent and Outcome
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: heatmap
:END:

Visualizes the distribution of crew actions by the agent they are
delegated to and the outcome of those actions, helping to identify
high-error or high-success patterns.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name crew_actions_by_agent_and_outcome :metric crew_actions :group_by [agent_to, crew_outcome]
SELECT agent_to, outcome AS crew_outcome, COUNT(*) AS crew_actions FROM crew_log GROUP BY agent_to, outcome
#+END_SRC

* Historical Events by Kind
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: area
:END:

Shows the count of historical events by kind over days, providing
insights into the frequency and types of events that occur, which can
inform content curation and maintenance.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name historical_events_by_kind :metric hist_kind_count :group_by [hist_kind, hist_day]
SELECT kind AS hist_kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10) AS hist_day, COUNT(DISTINCT kind) AS hist_kind_count FROM history GROUP BY kind, substr(timestamp, 1, 10)
#+END_SRC

* Sensor Readings by Probe Status
:PROPERTIES:
:VIZ_TYPE: bar
:END:

Displays the number of sensor readings by probe and status, helping to
identify issues with specific sensors or probes and ensuring data
integrity.

#+BEGIN_SRC sql :name sensor_readings_by_probe_status :metric sensor_readings :group_by [probe, probe_status]
SELECT probe, status AS probe_status, COUNT(*) AS sensor_readings FROM sensor_log GROUP BY probe, status
#+END_SRC
